---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../utils/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for Cozy Tiny Space — what data this site collects, cookies, analytics, advertising and your privacy rights."
  canonicalPath="/privacy-policy/"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Privacy Policy', url: '/privacy-policy/' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-4 pt-10">
    <h1 class="font-display text-[clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem)] font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[0.9rem] text-muted">Last updated: November 21, 2026</p>
    <div class="article-body mt-6">
      <p>
        Cozy Tiny Space ("we", "us", "our") is a content website about
        renter-friendly storage and organization. This policy explains what
        information we collect, how we use it, and the choices you have.
      </p>
      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not run user accounts and does not ask you to register.
        The only personal information you may give us directly is your name,
        email address and message if you contact us at
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}> {SITE.email}</a>. We use it only to
        reply to you. We do not sell, rent or share your email address.
      </p>
      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We and our partners use cookies and similar technologies (such as
        pixels and local storage) to run the site, measure visits and serve
        advertising. Some cookies are set by third-party vendors, including
        Google and our advertising partners, as described in the Advertising
        section below. You can block or delete cookies in your browser
        settings at any time; the site will still work, though ads may be
        less relevant.
      </p>
      <h2>Consent</h2>
      <p>
        If you visit from the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or
        Switzerland, you will be shown a consent banner provided through a
        certified consent management platform. Advertising and analytics
        cookies that need consent are only used after you give it, and you
        can withdraw consent at any time through the banner settings or your
        browser.
      </p>
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to understand which guides readers
        find useful. It is a privacy-friendly tool that does not use cookies
        and does not identify individual visitors; it reports aggregated
        usage data such as pages visited, approximate country and device
        type.
      </p>
      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        This site displays advertising served by Mediavine Journey and may
        also use Google AdSense. Third-party vendors, including Google, use
        cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this website and
        other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and
        its partners to serve ads based on your visits to this site and/or
        other sites on the Internet.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may opt out of personalised advertising by visiting
        <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener"> Google Ads Settings</a>.
        You can also opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for
        personalised advertising at
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"> aboutads.info/choices</a>
        (US) or
        <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"> youronlinechoices.eu</a>
        (Europe). Opting out does not stop ads; it stops them being
        personalised.
      </p>
      <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        This site currently contains no affiliate links. If affiliate links
        are added in the future, they will be clearly identified and this
        policy and the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a>
        will be updated first.
      </p>
      <h2>Third-party links</h2>
      <p>
        Our articles link to third-party websites (manufacturers, publishers
        and reference sources). We are not responsible for their privacy
        practices. Please read their policies when you visit them.
      </p>
      <h2>Your rights — EEA and UK (GDPR)</h2>
      <p>
        If you are in the EEA or UK, you have the right to access, correct,
        delete or restrict the personal data we hold about you, to object to
        its processing, and to data portability. We process contact emails
        on the basis of our legitimate interest in replying to you, and
        consent-based cookies only with your consent. To exercise any right,
        email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and we will
        respond within one month.
      </p>
      <h2>Your rights — California (CCPA/CPRA)</h2>
      <p>
        If you are a California resident, you have the right to know what
        personal information we collect, to request its deletion, and to opt
        out of its sale or sharing. We do not sell personal information. Our
        advertising partners' use of cookies may count as "sharing" for
        cross-context behavioural advertising under California law; you can
        opt out through the consent and opt-out links above or by emailing
        us. We will not discriminate against you for exercising these rights.
      </p>
      <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        This site is intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect
        personal information from children under 13 (or under 16 in the
        EEA).
      </p>
      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy when the site changes. The "Last updated"
        date above will change, and material changes will be noted here.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
